# Lesson 5, new exercise: after 2♥, responder raises to game.
title: A heart fit, and game values
id: L05-17
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.4
student: S
board: 36
dealer: W
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AK4    AK82   K632   75
  E  QT653  93     QJ7    T92
  S  2      QJT6   AT84   KJ43
  W  J987   754    95     AQ86

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 2C*    = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
     key: Four hearts and 11 points: Stayman.
     not 3NT: You have four hearts. Check for a fit first.
  W Pass
  N 2H     = Four hearts
  E Pass
  S 4H*    = Game in hearts
     key: A heart fit and enough for game: bid 4♥.
     not 3H: 3♥ only invites. With 11 you have enough for game.
     not 3NT: You've found an 8-card heart fit. Play in hearts.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner showed four hearts, and with 11 points you knew there was a game.
  North is declarer, because North bid hearts first, and so East will lead to
  the first trick.

play:
  1   E DQ  S D4  W D5  N DK
  2   N HA  E H3  S H6  W H4
      note: Declarer's plan: draw trumps, then ruff the spade loser in dummy. Start with the ♥A.
  3   N HK  E H9  S HT  W H5
      note: Keep drawing trumps.
  4   N H2  E S3  S HQ  W H7
      note: The last trump, won in dummy. Dummy keeps the ♥J for a spade ruff.
  5   S S2  W S7  N SA  E S5
      note: Dummy leads its spade to declarer's ace.
  6   N SK  E S6  S C3  W S8
      note: Cash the ♠K. Dummy has no spades left, so it throws a club.
  7   N S4  E ST  S HJ  W S9
      note: Ruff the last spade in dummy.
  8   S CK  W CA  N C5  E C2
      note: Lead the ♣K to drive out the ace and set up the ♣J.
  9   W CQ  N C7  E C9  S C4
  10  W C8  N H8  E CT  S CJ
      note: Declarer ruffs, even though dummy's ♣J would win, to be in hand to lead diamonds toward dummy.
  11  N D6  E D7  S DT  W D9
      note: Lead toward dummy's A-T-8. East's lead of the ♦Q promised the ♦J, so the 10 is worth trying.
  12  S DA  W C6  N D2  E DJ
      note: Cash the ♦A, and the jack falls.
  13  S D8  W SJ  N D3  E SQ
      note: Dummy's ♦8 is good. 11 tricks: 4♥ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: draw trumps, then ruff the spade loser in dummy. Dummy's
  singleton spade makes that possible, and it needs one trump left in dummy.

  4♥ made eleven tricks. 3NT would have taken only nine or ten: in no-trump
  the spade loser can't be ruffed. With a 4-4 major fit, the suit contract
  usually takes at least one trick more.
